<section class="how-does-it-work-section">
    <h2>How <em>exactly</em> does that <em>work?</em></h2>
    <p class="how-does-it-work-text-content">
        <b>Just send messages like you normally would.</b>
        Once in a while Jstmemit picks a meme template, takes some GIFs, messages and mixes it all together. Resulted meme
        is sent into your channel without you having to do anything.
    </p>
    <img
        src="https://files.jstmemit.com/jstmemit/images/topgg/howDoesItWork.png"
        alt="illustration of how mixing separate messages into one meme text works"
    />
</section>

<style>
    .how-does-it-work-section {
        background-color: var(--color-ash-black);
        display: flex;
        justify-content: center;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 1rem;
        position: relative;
        padding: 3.5rem 2rem 2rem;
        border-radius: 0.5rem 0.5rem 2rem 2rem;
        margin-top: 4rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--color-bubblegum-pink);
    }

    .how-does-it-work-section h2 {
        position: absolute;
        padding: 1rem;
        background-color: var(--color-ash-black);
        border-radius: 0.8rem;
        border: 2px solid var(--color-bubblegum-pink);

        font-weight: 800;
        font-size: 1.5rem;

        top: -4rem;
    }

    p.how-does-it-work-text-content {
        color: #d4d4d4;
        line-height: 1.75rem;
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.6rem;
        flex-direction: column;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    p.how-does-it-work-text-content > b {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        color: #fff;
    }

    .how-does-it-work-section img {
        width: 100%;
        margin-left: 1rem;
        padding-bottom: 1rem;
    }
</style>
